  "worked_solution": "Approaching from the left, we have $x<3,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{3x-1}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}\\sqrt[3]{3x-1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{3\\cdot 3-1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{8} \\\\  & =2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApproaching from the right, we have $x>3,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x\\pi ).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3\\pi ) \\\\  & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the two limits are different, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)=\\text{DNE}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
